{"strongs": "H5104", "word": "נָהָר", "translit": "na.har", "root": "הי", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "stream, river", "definition": "נָהָר noun masculine Gen 2:10 stream, river ; — absolute ׳ נ Gen 2:10 +; construct נְהַר Deut 1:7 +; plural נְהָרִים Isa 18:27 + 4 t., construct נַהֲרֵי Isa 18:1 + 2 t; but oftener נְהָר(וֺ)ת Isa 19:6 + 23 t.; construct נַהֲרוֺת 2Kgs 5:12 + 2 t.; suffix נַהֲרוֺהֶיךָ Ezek 32:2 , נַהֲרֹתַיִךְ Isa 44:27 , נַהֲרֹתֶיהָ Ezek 31:4 ; Ezek 31:15 , נַהֲרֹתָם Exod 7:19 , נַהֲרוֺתָם Ezek 32:2 ; Ezek 32:14 apparently dual נַהֲרַיִם Gen 24:10 + 2 t., נַהֲרָ֑יִם Judg 3:8 (see below) (all in ׳ אֲרַם נ ); — 1. stream, river , Num 24:6 ( J E ), Job 14:11 ; Job 40:23 ; Ps 105:41 (in simile), Isa 48:18 (id.), Isa 59:19 (id.) + often; frequently of particular rivers; r. of Eden Gen 2:10 and its branches v Gen 2:13 v Gen 2:14 (all J ); נְהַר מִצְרַיִם Gen 15:18 ( J ; i.e., si vera 1., the Nile) but read probably ׳ נַחַל מ , whence נהר through influence of following נהר — compare 2Kgs 24:7 — Nö ZMG xi.1886, 699 (alternative), Lag BN 140 Ball Hpt ; נָהָר of Nile Isa 19:5 especially of Euphrates נְהַר פְּרָת Gen 15:18 ; Deut 1:7 (both + הַגָּדוֺל ׳ הַנּ ) Josh 1:4 + 8 t. + 2Sam 8:3 ( Qr ᵐ5 and || 1Chr 18:3 Kt omit פְּרָת ; — compare also Gen 2:14 b above); oftener (of Euphrase) without ׳ הַנָּהָר ׃פ κατ’ ἐξοχήν , Gen 31:21 ; Exod 23:31 ; Num 22:5 ; Josh 24:2 ; Josh 24:3 ; Josh 24:14 ; Josh 24:15 (all E ), possibly also Gen 36:37 ( P ; compare Di ) = 1Chr 1:48 , + 13 t. + 2Sam 8:3 Kt (see above); and even without article (poetry) Isa 7:20 ; Jer 2:18 ; Mic 7:12 ; Zech 9:10 ; Ps 72:8 ׳ הַגּ ׳ הַנּ once of Tigris Dan 10:4 נְהַר גוֺזָן ( חבור ) 2Kgs 17:6 ; 2Kgs 18:11 compare 2Chr 5:26 plural נַהֲרֵי בוּשׁ Zeph 3:10 perhaps of a canal: נְהַרכְּֿבָר Ezek 1:1 ; Ezek 1:3 + 6 t. Ezekiel; הַנָּהָר אַהֲלוא Ezra 8:21 , ׳ נְהַר א v Ezra 8:31 compare נַהֲרוֺת בָּבֶל Ps 137:1 canals possibly also in ׳ שַׁעֲרֵי הַנּ Nah 2:7 (of Nineveh); of canals of Egypt Exod 7:19 (|| יְאֹרִים etc.), Exod 8:1 (|| id.). 2. נְהָרוֺת ( מִבְּכִי ) Job 28:11 usually understood of (underground) streams ; Szold Comm. Job Gr Monatsschr.1887, 410 and Perles Analekten 69 proposes ׳ נ ׳ נִבְכֵ sources of rivers (compare Job 36:16 ); Wetzst Hoffm Bu ׳ נ ׳ מַבְּכֵ (not elsewhere) with similar meaning. 3. figurative of ׳ י s favour Ps 46:5 . — On נַהֲרַיִם ending apparently dual, see אֲרַם ; Tel Amarna Na-ri-ma, Na—rima ( Wkl Tel Am. 40 *), and Egyptian Nhrina ( WMM As.u.Eur.249ff. ) point however to original ending יִ֯ם ; this inconsistent with view of EMey Geschichte. § 180 that יִַ֯ם here a locative ending (compare Ba § 194 c. Anm. l Buhl Ges 12 ), see also Di Gen 24:10 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5024')\">BDB5024</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H5104')\">H5104</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5023')\">BDB5023</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5025')\">BDB5025</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>נָהָר</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Gen 2:10\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(1,2,10)\">Gen 2:10</ref></sup> <highlightword>stream, river</highlightword>; — absolute <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>נ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 2:10\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(1,2,10)\">Gen 2:10</ref> +; construct <bdbheb>נְהַר</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 1:7\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(5,1,7)\">Deut 1:7</ref> +; plural <bdbheb>נְהָרִים</bdbheb> <checkingNeeded/><ref ref=\"Isa 18:27\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"27\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"27\" onclick=\"bcv(23,18,27)\">Isa 18:27</ref> + 4 t., construct <bdbheb>נַהֲרֵי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 18:1\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(23,18,1)\">Isa 18:1</ref> + 2 t; but oftener <bdbheb>נְהָר(וֺ)ת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 19:6\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(23,19,6)\">Isa 19:6</ref> + 23 t.; construct <bdbheb>נַהֲרוֺת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Kgs 5:12\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(12,5,12)\">2Kgs 5:12</ref> + 2 t.; suffix <bdbheb>נַהֲרוֺהֶיךָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 32:2\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(26,32,2)\">Ezek 32:2</ref>, <bdbheb>נַהֲרֹתַיִךְ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 44:27\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"44\" vBegin=\"27\" cEnd=\"44\" vEnd=\"27\" onclick=\"bcv(23,44,27)\">Isa 44:27</ref>, <bdbheb>נַהֲרֹתֶיהָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 31:4\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(26,31,4)\">Ezek 31:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 31:15\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(26,31,15)\">Ezek 31:15</ref>, <bdbheb>נַהֲרֹתָם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 7:19\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(2,7,19)\">Exod 7:19</ref>, <bdbheb>נַהֲרוֺתָם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 32:2\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(26,32,2)\">Ezek 32:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 32:14\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(26,32,14)\">Ezek 32:14</ref> apparently dual <bdbheb>נַהֲרַיִם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 24:10\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(1,24,10)\">Gen 24:10</ref> + 2 t., <bdbheb>נַהֲרָ֑יִם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Judg 3:8\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(7,3,8)\">Judg 3:8</ref> (see below) (all in <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>אֲרַם נ</bdbheb>); — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlight>stream, river</highlight>, <ref ref=\"Num 24:6\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(4,24,6)\">Num 24:6</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup><lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Job 14:11\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(18,14,11)\">Job 14:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Job 40:23\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"40\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"40\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(18,40,23)\">Job 40:23</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 105:41\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"105\" vBegin=\"41\" cEnd=\"105\" vEnd=\"41\" onclick=\"bcv(19,105,41)\">Ps 105:41</ref> (in simile), <ref ref=\"Isa 48:18\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(23,48,18)\">Isa 48:18</ref> (id.), <ref ref=\"Isa 59:19\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"59\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"59\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(23,59,19)\">Isa 59:19</ref> (id.) + often; frequently of particular rivers; r. of Eden <ref ref=\"Gen 2:10\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(1,2,10)\">Gen 2:10</ref> and its branches v<ref ref=\"Gen 2:13\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(1,2,13)\">Gen 2:13</ref> v<ref ref=\"Gen 2:14\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(1,2,14)\">Gen 2:14</ref> (all <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup>); <bdbheb>נְהַר מִצְרַיִם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 15:18\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(1,15,18)\">Gen 15:18</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup>; i.e., si vera 1., the Nile) but read probably <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>נַחַל מ</bdbheb>, whence <bdbheb>נהר</bdbheb> through influence of following <bdbheb>נהר</bdbheb> — compare <ref ref=\"2Kgs 24:7\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(12,24,7)\">2Kgs 24:7</ref> — <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Nö')\">Nö<sup>ZMG xi.1886, 699</sup></lookup> (alternative), <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Lag')\">Lag<sup>BN 140</sup></lookup> Ball<sup>Hpt</sup>; <bdbheb>נָהָר</bdbheb> of Nile <ref ref=\"Isa 19:5\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(23,19,5)\">Isa 19:5</ref> especially of Euphrates <bdbheb>נְהַר פְ